{%- comment -%}
  The two built-in question sets, the ones Fergal approved on 30 September 2026 by
  adopting the old website's approach (setup/old-site-questionnaires.md).

  Unlike the pharmacy.questionnaire metaobject, these are not edited per product:
  they are chosen by tag in sections/main-product.liquid, so a newly tagged medicine
  gets its questions the moment it is tagged and nobody has to remember a metafield.

  The ED set is the old site's 14, tidied and then extended on 30 Sep 2026 on Fergal's
  instruction that our approved draft fills the gaps the old site leaves:
    - three spellings corrected (riocigaut, protsate, non-artertic);
    - punctuation corrected, meaning untouched (spaces before question marks and after
      commas, "e.g.", and the bracket question 12 never closed);
    - question 4, which broke off mid-sentence on the old site, replaced with the
      wording Fergal supplied, drawn from our draft's set 1;
    - questions 15 to 18 added from our draft's set 1, because the old site asks
      nothing equivalent. They are marked in MAINTENANCE.md.
  Questions 1-3 and 5-14 are still the old site's own wording.
  The verbatim, uncorrected original is in setup/old-site-questionnaires.md and must
  stay that way: it records what the old site asks, not what we ask.

  Output: one line per question, `kind::label`, questions joined by '||'.
  Kinds: yes_no | confirm | yes_no_details (Yes reveals a free-text box).
  Neither set has blocking answers — Fergal's decision is that no answer stops the
  sale; the pharmacist reads the answers on the order and decides. See
  MAINTENANCE.md, "Questions before purchase follow the tag" .

  Accepts: set — 'ed' or 'default'.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- case set -%}
  {%- when 'ed' -%}
yes_no::Has your doctor advised that you are not fit enough for any physical and/or sexual activity?||yes_no::Do you feel very breathless or experience chest pain with light or moderate physical activity, such as walking briskly for 20 minutes or climbing two flights of stairs?||yes_no::Have you had a heart attack or stroke within the last 6 months?||yes_no::Do you have any other heart problems, or are you under a doctor's care for any of the following: a heart attack, stroke, unstable angina or severe heart failure in the last 6 months; chest pain or breathlessness with light exercise (such as climbing two flights of stairs); low blood pressure; or severe liver disease?||yes_no::Are you taking nitrates (nicorandil or other nitric oxide donors e.g. glyceryl trinitrate, isosorbide mononitrate or isosorbide dinitrate) for chest pain?||yes_no::Are you using drugs called 'poppers' for recreational purposes (e.g. amyl nitrite)?||yes_no::Are you taking riociguat or other guanylate cyclase stimulators for lung problems?||yes_no::Are you taking ritonavir (for HIV infection)?||yes_no::Are you taking any CYP3A4 inhibitors, e.g. saquinavir (to treat HIV infection), cimetidine (a heartburn treatment), itraconazole or ketoconazole (to treat fungal infections), erythromycin or rifampicin (antibiotics) or diltiazem (for high blood pressure)?||yes_no::Are you taking any alpha-blockers, such as alfuzosin, doxazosin or tamsulosin, which are medicines to treat urinary problems due to enlarged prostate (benign prostatic hyperplasia) or occasionally to treat high blood pressure?||yes_no::Do you have Peyronie's disease or any other deformation of the penis?||yes_no::Have you ever had loss of vision because of damage to the optic nerve (such as non-arteritic ischaemic optic neuropathy [NAION]), or have an inherited eye disease (such as retinitis pigmentosa)?||yes_no::Do you have galactose intolerance, Lapp lactase deficiency or glucose-galactose malabsorption?||yes_no::Do you have previously diagnosed hepatic (liver) disease (including cirrhosis of the liver) or severe renal (kidney) impairment?||yes_no::Is this medicine for a man aged 18 or over who has difficulty getting or keeping an erection?||yes_no::Do you take any medicine for high blood pressure or for the prostate, other than the ones already listed above?||yes_no::Do you take any medicine for HIV, other than the ones already listed above?||yes_no::Do you have sickle cell disease, leukaemia, myeloma, a bleeding disorder, or an active stomach ulcer?
  {%- when 'default' -%}
confirm::I am over 18 years of age||yes_no_details::Are you taking any other medication?
{%- endcase -%}
